# Deny everything, then allow only what the Dockerfile actually COPYs.
#
# Deliberately an allowlist. The context otherwise included montrek/uploads
# (customer files) and db_backups (database dumps) -- 18GB shipped to the daemon on
# every build, and one `COPY . .` away from being baked into an image that gets
# pushed to a registry.
#
# If you add a COPY/ADD to Dockerfile or Dockerfile.app, add a matching `!` line
# here or the build will fail with "file not found".
*

!bin/entrypoints/montrek-entrypoint.sh

# Dockerfile.app: the code and the requirements. A re-included directory comes
# back whole, so everything under it that is runtime data, a local artefact or
# an extension checked out into a dev tree is excluded again after it -- later
# lines win.
!bin
!montrek
!requirements.in
!requirements.txt
montrek/uploads
montrek/sent_emails
montrek/reporting/.workbench
montrek/mt_*
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/.coverage
**/.scannerwork
**/node_modules
